---
description: Trigger patch - a content edit to any .md misses the doc skills' keyword triggers, so this glob routes it.
globs: "**/*.md"
alwaysApply: false
---

Authoring or restructuring any .md (README, ADR, runbook):
the FIRST action after this rule attaches is the `markdown-style` Skill call, before the NEXT write
to that file lands; its own keywords only catch explicit lint asks, so a content edit misses it. ADR,
Mermaid-diagram or C4 work loads `docs-as-code` in that SAME first action, on top of it - same blind
spot, one first action, not two competing ones. Skip one-line tweaks.

**When this rule reaches you it is already too late for the write that triggered it** - a
path-scoped rule attaches ON a file touch, measured 9.9 s AFTER the edit it governs, so the load is
a precondition of the SKILL that owns the deliverable, not of this rule. A run working through the
shell gets no attach at all until it uses a file tool (measured: 0 attaches over 123 `.md` write
targets), and nothing on this platform announces it - load this rule yourself on the first shell
touch of a `.md` file.

**The generated docs root is NOT governed here.** Every document under `<docs-path>` belongs to the
capture skill that writes it, and that skill's own body states the shape and loads `markdown-style`
itself. Two owners pulling one file in opposite directions is worse than either alone, and the
attach here was obeyed in only 1 of 2 identical runs - neither a reliable gate nor a free one.
